---
import Layout from '../../../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import '../../../../styles/ai.css';
---

<Layout
  title="GPT-5.6 Sol — A.I. — Rycode"
  description="OpenAI's flagship for complex professional work."
  variant="ai"
>
  <article class="ai-model">
    <p class="ai-model-kicker">Frontier models</p>
    <h1 class="ai-model-title">GPT-5.6 Sol</h1>
    <p class="ai-model-dek">GPT-5.6 Sol is OpenAI’s prior flagship for complex professional work and was the pre-Astra default for many teams. The model id is <code>gpt-5.6-sol</code> (alias <code>gpt-5.6</code>). Pricing is $4 input and $20 output per million tokens. Knowledge cutoff is February 16, 2026.</p>
    <hr class="ai-model-rule" />
    <h2 class="ai-model-section">Training</h2>
    <p>Knowledge cutoff is February 16, 2026. Parameter count, training FLOPs, and the train-time RL recipe for Sol are not published on the Sol model page.</p>
    <h2 class="ai-model-section">Inference</h2>
    <p><code>reasoning.effort</code> includes <code>none</code> through <code>max</code> (broader than Astra, which has no <code>none</code>). Reasoning tokens are supported.</p>
    <h2 class="ai-model-section">Context</h2>
    <p>The documented context window is 1.05 million tokens. Max output is 128K tokens.</p>
    <h2 class="ai-model-section">Methods</h2>
    <p>Functions, web search, file search, and computer use are named on the models page.</p>
    <h2 class="ai-model-section">Benchmarking</h2>
    <p>OpenAI-published Sol numbers from the GPT-6 Astra announce (OpenAI’s Sol column). Anthropic’s Fable page also prints a Sol column under Anthropic’s harness; those are separate prints.</p>
    <div class="ai-model-table-wrap">
      <table class="ai-model-table ai-model-table--prose">
        <thead><tr><th scope="col">Eval</th><th scope="col">GPT-5.6 Sol (OpenAI)</th><th scope="col">GPT-6 Astra</th><th scope="col">Notes</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>Terminal-Bench 4.0</td><td>37.3%</td><td>57.9%</td><td></td></tr>
          <tr><td>Terminal-Bench Science 0.1</td><td>22.4%</td><td>64.6%</td><td></td></tr>
          <tr><td>OSWorld 2.0 (latency sim prose)</td><td>65.7% @ ~75 min/task</td><td>72.6% @ ~40 min</td><td>Astra ~47% less time</td></tr>
          <tr><td>AutomationBench</td><td>18.1%</td><td>41.4%</td><td></td></tr>
          <tr><td>BrowseComp</td><td>90.4%</td><td>91.5%</td><td></td></tr>
          <tr><td>BenchCAD</td><td>83.3%</td><td>95.9%</td><td></td></tr>
          <tr><td>DeepSWE v1.1</td><td>72.7%</td><td>74.1%</td><td></td></tr>
          <tr><td>FrontierMath Tier 4 (v2)</td><td>83.0%</td><td>97.6%</td><td></td></tr>
          <tr><td>GPQA Diamond</td><td>94.6%</td><td>96.0%</td><td></td></tr>
          <tr><td>Humanity&#x27;s Last Exam (w/ tools)</td><td>-</td><td>57.2%</td><td>Sol not listed for this row</td></tr>
        </tbody></table></div>
    <p>Health (system card Table 6, length-adjusted, Sol as baseline): HealthBench Professional 60.5; HealthBench 57.0; HealthBench Hard 33.1.</p>
    <p>Anthropic also printed GPT-5.6 Sol columns on the Fable 5.1 announce for some evals (for example Terminal-Bench 4.0 at 37.3%, AutomationBench at 19.6%, CursorBench 3.2.0 at 67.2%). Those are Anthropic’s harness results and are not merged into the table above.</p>
    <h2 class="ai-model-section">Hardware</h2>
    <p>OpenAI has not published training or serving silicon details for Sol on the model docs. OpenAI’s published Stargate Abilene / NVIDIA GB200 naming applies to GPT-5.5 training, not a Sol-specific map. Buyers purchase API tokens.</p>
    <h2 class="ai-model-section">Access and pricing</h2>
    <p>Pricing is $4 input and $20 output per million tokens. Sibling GPT-5.6 Terra (<code>gpt-5.6-terra</code>) is $2 / $12 with the same 1.05M / 128K context and output shape and the same February 16, 2026 cutoff. Sibling GPT-5.6 Luna (<code>gpt-5.6-luna</code>) is $0.20 / $1.20 with cached input at $0.02; <code>reasoning.effort</code> supports <code>none</code>, <code>low</code>, <code>medium</code> (default), <code>high</code>, <code>xhigh</code>, and <code>max</code> on the Luna model page. Lab score tables for Terra and Luna are not on the pages cited here.</p>
